{"version": 2, "width": 104, "height": 34, "timestamp": 1793426520, "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}, "title": "AEGIS in about a minute"}
[0.389, "o", "\u001b[1mAEGIS: an autonomous defence agent for a web app\u001b[0m   (free, local, open source)\r\nThe app: BookNook, a small shop with a login page, on port 3000.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36m[1/5]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mPut AEGIS in front of the app\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m$ aegis init --target http://127.0.0.1:3000 --shadow-s 8 --canary-s 12\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.463, "o", "  wrote aegis.json: protecting http://127.0.0.1:3000 on 127.0.0.1:8080\r\n  next:  aegis doctor   then   aegis learn\r\n\u001b[32m$ aegis learn\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.079, "o", "  LEARN mode: AEGIS is in front of http://127.0.0.1:3000 on http://127.0.0.1:8080  - it never blocks anything.\r\n  Send your normal traffic through that address (real users, your test-suite, a staging copy).\r\n  When `aegis status` shows >= 2000 requests, run: aegis protect\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36m[2/5]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mLet it watch normal traffic first (it never blocks while learning)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.586, "o", "  ... 496 requests from ordinary visitors"]
[2.586, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.087, "o", "  ... 1,031 requests from ordinary visitors"]
[4.087, "o", "\r\n"]
[5.587, "o", "  ... 1,543 requests from ordinary visitors\r\n"]
[7.087, "o", "  ... 2,072 requests from ordinary visitors\r\n"]
[8.63, "o", "  ... 2,409 requests from ordinary visitors\r\n"]
[9.631, "o", "\u001b[32m$ aegis protect\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.759, "o", "  PROTECT mode: gateway enforcing on http://127.0.0.1:8080, controller watching for campaigns.\r\n  Gate evidence: 2398 learned requests from 481 visitors. New rules go shadow -> canary -> enforce, and roll back automatically.\r\n  WARNING: 2.1% of learned requests (51) look like attacks. If that is not normal for your app, learning overlapped an attack: re-learn on trusted traff\r\n  NOTE: gate windows shortened (shadow 8s, canary 12s; defaults 30s/45s). Every stage still runs, but a rule is watched for less time before it enforces\r\n  Watch it with: aegis events -f     Summary: aegis status\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36m[3/5]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mProtection is on. Now an attack that looks like normal traffic\u001b[0m\r\n  A bot replays leaked passwords against /api/login, ~8 guesses a second.\r\n  Each request is an ordinary login: the standard WAF rules (OWASP CRS) see nothing wrong.\r\n\r\n"]
[11.771, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m[4/5]\u001b[0m \u001b[1mAEGIS on its own (nobody touches anything now)\u001b[0m"]
[11.772, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.173, "o", "\u001b[33m        bot so far: 3 guesses | 3 reached the app | 0 stopped by AEGIS | real accounts found: 0\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.973, "o", "  \u001b[2m+   1s\u001b[0m CAMPAIGN  credential_stuffing by h:f8093b12cb488d55 (8 requests, detected 0.7s after it began)\r\n  \u001b[2m+   1s\u001b[0m gate      candidate aegis-credential_stuffing-1: passed\r\n"]
[12.973, "o", "  \u001b[2m+   1s\u001b[0m RULE      made aegis-credential_stuffing-1 [fresh] in 0.01s\r\n"]
[12.973, "o", "  \u001b[2m+   1s\u001b[0m live      aegis-credential_stuffing-1 on real traffic: shadow 8s, then canary 12s at 25%\r\n"]
[15.375, "o", "\u001b[33m        bot so far: 28 guesses | 28 reached the app | 0 stopped by AEGIS | real accounts found: 1\u001b[0m\r\n"]
